## Lore

The D''norr are called Devilmen for their looks: reddish-tan bipeds whose
gourd-shaped heads are darker red on males and purple on females and dotted
with tiny red spines, with dark blue eyes, gnarled pointed ears, a pair of
forehead horns and short spines over the brows (and on the chins of males).

The resemblance stops at the surface. D''norr are thoughtful, gentle and
deeply curious, devoted to philosophy, the arts, learning and debate, and
they prefer peaceful answers to every problem. A third are true pacifists
who fight only to protect themselves or the innocent. They make natural
teachers, negotiators and diplomats, and have won the respect of
Cyber-Knights, Justice Rangers, Tundra Rangers and New West lawmen, and a
welcome among Native Americans, Fennodi, Lyn-Srial, Psi-Stalkers and even
the Simvan.

Their home world had no magic, so the very idea fascinates them, and half
of all Devilmen take up a magic O.C.C. Their natural store of P.P.E. makes
them prized prey for Psi-Stalkers and other energy vampires, and their
magic puts them near the top of the Coalition''s extermination list. Many
fought and died for Tolkeen.

## GM Notes

Pronounced Duh nor; also called Melonheads by Coalition soldiers, Devils,
and Horned Red Brother by many Native Americans. Size 5-6 feet (1.5 to 1.8
m); weight 120 to 180 lbs (54 to 81 kg), slender. Life span 5D6+170 years;
mature at 18; one child after a nine month pregnancy, up to age 80.

Habitat: throughout the Americas, most numerous at Tolkeen (before its
fall), Lazlo, New Lazlo and the Midwest; some in the Magic Zone and
Atlantis, where those foolish enough to visit are enslaved. A few selfish or
evil Devilman mages belong to the Federation of Magic. Many refugees of
Tolkeen now protect and care for other refugees.

Allies: many friends; respected by Cyber-Knights, lawmen and anyone who
knows them as honorable. Enemies: the Coalition States, monsters, villains
and cutthroats, Psi-Stalkers and other P.P.E. vampires, though even
Psi-Stalkers who come to know them grow to like them.
